<fdm_config name="c172" version="2.0" release="BETA"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="http://jsbsim.sourceforge.net/JSBSim.xsd">

    <fileheader>
        <author> Unknown </author>
        <filecreationdate>2002-01-01</filecreationdate>
        <version> $Id: c172p.xml,v 1.29 2013/10/25 15:32:49 jentron Exp $ </version>
        <description> Cessna C-172 (modified for the TeachX Flight Simulator) </description>
      <note>
        This model was created using publicly available data, publicly available
        technical reports, textbooks, and guesses. It contains no proprietary or
        restricted data. If this model has been validated at all, it would be
        only to the extent that it seems to "fly right", and that it possibly
        complies with published, publicly known, performance data (maximum speed,
        endurance, etc.). Thus, this model is meant for educational and entertainment
        purposes only.

        This simulation model is not endorsed by the manufacturer. This model is not
        to be sold.
      </note>
      <note>
        MODIFIED FILE. This is JSBSim's aircraft/c172p/c172p.xml changed by the TeachX Flight
        Simulator project (2026) to match Cessna 172P handbook-class performance and to teach
        correct handling habits (rigging, left-turning tendencies, stalls, spins, ground handling).
        Every change is listed in flightsim/jsbsim/CHANGES.md; the unmodified original is kept in
        flightsim/jsbsim/upstream/. The tables between the TEACHX-GENERATED markers are written by
        flightsim/jsbsim/tools/gen_model.py (edit the parameters there, not the numbers here).
        It is a learning aid, not validated flight-training data.
      </note>
    </fileheader>

